  "id": "COMPOUND:20725 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "Gardenoside appears to interact with M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through a series of target relationships, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the modulation of cellular processes associated with the M-phase. The evidence indicates that Gardenoside targets SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, Tetraethylammonium, and 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one. These compounds all share the common effect of targeting M-phase phosphoprotein 8, implying a possible pathway where Gardenoside may influence the same molecular targets through different mechanisms. The integration of these relationships highlights the possibility that Gardenoside exerts its effects by modulating the activity of M-phase phosphoprotein 8, potentially through the inhibition or activation of key regulatory processes in the cell cycle. The consistent targeting of SNU-387 by multiple compounds suggests a broader role in the biological response to these agents, reinforcing the hypothesis that Gardenoside may act as a modulator of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through a shared target network.",
